{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"heading","depth":1,"id":"react","children":[{"type":"text","value":"React"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The React adapter renders Markdown source or a pre-parsed document without an intermediate HTML string."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"component-usage","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Component usage"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { Markdown } from '@tanstack/markdown/react'\n\nexport function Article({ source }: { source: string }) {\n  return <Markdown>{source}</Markdown>\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Markdown"},{"type":"text","value":" returns a fragment, so the surrounding semantic element remains under application control."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"replace-intrinsic-elements","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Replace intrinsic elements"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Map an HTML tag name to a component or another tag:"}]},{"type":"component","name":"live-example","tagName":"md-live-example","attributes":{"id":"react-components-1"},"properties":{"data-example-group":"react-components","data-collapsed-indexes":"[]","data-workspace":"{\"version\":1,\"entry\":\"/src/main.tsx\",\"environment\":\"react\",\"files\":{\"/src/main.tsx\":\"import {\\n  Markdown,\\n  type MarkdownComponents,\\n} from '@tanstack/markdown/react'\\n\\nconst source = `# Project links\\n\\n- [TanStack](https://tanstack.com)\\n- [Documentation](/docs)\\n\\n![TanStack logo](https://tanstack.com/images/logo-color-100.png)`\\n\\nconst components = {\\n  a(props) {\\n    const hasProtocol = /^[a-z][a-z0-9+.-]*:/i.test(props.href || '')\\n    const allowed =\\n      !hasProtocol || /^(https?:|mailto:)/i.test(props.href || '')\\n    const href = allowed ? props.href : undefined\\n    const external = /^https?:\\\\/\\\\//i.test(href || '')\\n\\n    return (\\n      <a\\n        {...props}\\n        href={href}\\n        rel={external ? 'nofollow noopener noreferrer' : props.rel}\\n        target={external ? '_blank' : props.target}\\n      />\\n    )\\n  },\\n  img({ alt }) {\\n    return <span role=\\\"img\\\">Image: {alt || 'No description'}</span>\\n  },\\n} satisfies MarkdownComponents\\n\\nexport default function Article() {\\n  return <Markdown components={components}>{source}</Markdown>\\n}\"}}"},"children":[{"type":"code","value":"import {\n  Markdown,\n  type MarkdownComponents,\n} from '@tanstack/markdown/react'\n\nconst source = `# Project links\n\n- [TanStack](https://tanstack.com)\n- [Documentation](/docs)\n\n![TanStack logo](https://tanstack.com/images/logo-color-100.png)`\n\nconst components = {\n  a(props) {\n    const hasProtocol = /^[a-z][a-z0-9+.-]*:/i.test(props.href || '')\n    const allowed =\n      !hasProtocol || /^(https?:|mailto:)/i.test(props.href || '')\n    const href = allowed ? props.href : undefined\n    const external = /^https?:\\/\\//i.test(href || '')\n\n    return (\n      <a\n        {...props}\n        href={href}\n        rel={external ? 'nofollow noopener noreferrer' : props.rel}\n        target={external ? '_blank' : props.target}\n      />\n    )\n  },\n  img({ alt }) {\n    return <span role=\"img\">Image: {alt || 'No description'}</span>\n  },\n} satisfies MarkdownComponents\n\nexport default function Article() {\n  return <Markdown components={components}>{source}</Markdown>\n}","lang":"tsx","meta":"group=react-components env=react file=/src/main.tsx entry","title":"/src/main.tsx","file":"/src/main.tsx"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Known intrinsic keys receive their matching React props by inference, so "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"a"},{"type":"text","value":" exposes anchor props and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"img"},{"type":"text","value":" exposes image props. Arbitrary extension component tag names remain supported. Mappings apply to every intrinsic tag emitted through the React renderer."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"pre-parse-for-ssr","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Pre-parse for SSR"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { parseMarkdown } from '@tanstack/markdown/parser'\nimport { Markdown } from '@tanstack/markdown/react'\n\nconst document = parseMarkdown(source)\n\nexport function Article() {\n  return <Markdown>{document}</Markdown>\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The AST contains no functions, classes, or environment-specific values. It can be built ahead of time or loaded from a content cache."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"lower-level-rendering","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Lower-level rendering"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"renderMarkdownReact"},{"type":"text","value":" outside JSX, or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"renderBlockReact"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"renderInlineReact"},{"type":"text","value":" when composing a custom renderer around the standard nodes."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"parity-and-keys","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Parity and keys"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The adapter generates deterministic keys from tree positions. Core SSR output is tested against the HTML renderer. Custom components, raw HTML, highlighter output, and HTML-only extension hooks are application-controlled boundaries and are not covered by that equivalence guarantee."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"react","text":"React","level":1},{"id":"component-usage","text":"Component usage","level":2},{"id":"replace-intrinsic-elements","text":"Replace intrinsic elements","level":2},{"id":"pre-parse-for-ssr","text":"Pre-parse for SSR","level":2},{"id":"lower-level-rendering","text":"Lower-level rendering","level":2},{"id":"parity-and-keys","text":"Parity and keys","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n# React\n\nThe React adapter renders Markdown source or a pre-parsed document without an intermediate HTML string.\n\n## Component usage\n\n```tsx\nimport { Markdown } from '@tanstack/markdown/react'\n\nexport function Article({ source }: { source: string }) {\n  return <Markdown>{source}</Markdown>\n}\n```\n\n`Markdown` returns a fragment, so the surrounding semantic element remains under application control.\n\n## Replace intrinsic elements\n\nMap an HTML tag name to a component or another tag:\n\n```tsx group=react-components env=react file=/src/main.tsx entry\nimport {\n  Markdown,\n  type MarkdownComponents,\n} from '@tanstack/markdown/react'\n\nconst source = `# Project links\n\n- [TanStack](https://tanstack.com)\n- [Documentation](/docs)\n\n![TanStack logo](https://tanstack.com/images/logo-color-100.png)`\n\nconst components = {\n  a(props) {\n    const hasProtocol = /^[a-z][a-z0-9+.-]*:/i.test(props.href || '')\n    const allowed =\n      !hasProtocol || /^(https?:|mailto:)/i.test(props.href || '')\n    const href = allowed ? props.href : undefined\n    const external = /^https?:\\/\\//i.test(href || '')\n\n    return (\n      <a\n        {...props}\n        href={href}\n        rel={external ? 'nofollow noopener noreferrer' : props.rel}\n        target={external ? '_blank' : props.target}\n      />\n    )\n  },\n  img({ alt }) {\n    return <span role=\"img\">Image: {alt || 'No description'}</span>\n  },\n} satisfies MarkdownComponents\n\nexport default function Article() {\n  return <Markdown components={components}>{source}</Markdown>\n}\n```\n\nKnown intrinsic keys receive their matching React props by inference, so `a` exposes anchor props and `img` exposes image props. Arbitrary extension component tag names remain supported. Mappings apply to every intrinsic tag emitted through the React renderer.\n\n## Pre-parse for SSR\n\n```tsx\nimport { parseMarkdown } from '@tanstack/markdown/parser'\nimport { Markdown } from '@tanstack/markdown/react'\n\nconst document = parseMarkdown(source)\n\nexport function Article() {\n  return <Markdown>{document}</Markdown>\n}\n```\n\nThe AST contains no functions, classes, or environment-specific values. It can be built ahead of time or loaded from a content cache.\n\n## Lower-level rendering\n\nUse `renderMarkdownReact` outside JSX, or `renderBlockReact` and `renderInlineReact` when composing a custom renderer around the standard nodes.\n\n## Parity and keys\n\nThe adapter generates deterministic keys from tree positions. Core SSR output is tested against the HTML renderer. Custom components, raw HTML, highlighter output, and HTML-only extension hooks are application-controlled boundaries and are not covered by that equivalence guarantee.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: React\n---\n\n# React\n\nThe React adapter renders Markdown source or a pre-parsed document without an intermediate HTML string.\n\n## Component usage\n\n```tsx\nimport { Markdown } from '@tanstack/markdown/react'\n\nexport function Article({ source }: { source: string }) {\n  return <Markdown>{source}</Markdown>\n}\n```\n\n`Markdown` returns a fragment, so the surrounding semantic element remains under application control.\n\n## Replace intrinsic elements\n\nMap an HTML tag name to a component or another tag:\n\n```tsx group=react-components env=react file=/src/main.tsx entry\nimport {\n  Markdown,\n  type MarkdownComponents,\n} from '@tanstack/markdown/react'\n\nconst source = `# Project links\n\n- [TanStack](https://tanstack.com)\n- [Documentation](/docs)\n\n![TanStack logo](https://tanstack.com/images/logo-color-100.png)`\n\nconst components = {\n  a(props) {\n    const hasProtocol = /^[a-z][a-z0-9+.-]*:/i.test(props.href || '')\n    const allowed =\n      !hasProtocol || /^(https?:|mailto:)/i.test(props.href || '')\n    const href = allowed ? props.href : undefined\n    const external = /^https?:\\/\\//i.test(href || '')\n\n    return (\n      <a\n        {...props}\n        href={href}\n        rel={external ? 'nofollow noopener noreferrer' : props.rel}\n        target={external ? '_blank' : props.target}\n      />\n    )\n  },\n  img({ alt }) {\n    return <span role=\"img\">Image: {alt || 'No description'}</span>\n  },\n} satisfies MarkdownComponents\n\nexport default function Article() {\n  return <Markdown components={components}>{source}</Markdown>\n}\n```\n\nKnown intrinsic keys receive their matching React props by inference, so `a` exposes anchor props and `img` exposes image props. Arbitrary extension component tag names remain supported. Mappings apply to every intrinsic tag emitted through the React renderer.\n\n## Pre-parse for SSR\n\n```tsx\nimport { parseMarkdown } from '@tanstack/markdown/parser'\nimport { Markdown } from '@tanstack/markdown/react'\n\nconst document = parseMarkdown(source)\n\nexport function Article() {\n  return <Markdown>{document}</Markdown>\n}\n```\n\nThe AST contains no functions, classes, or environment-specific values. It can be built ahead of time or loaded from a content cache.\n\n## Lower-level rendering\n\nUse `renderMarkdownReact` outside JSX, or `renderBlockReact` and `renderInlineReact` when composing a custom renderer around the standard nodes.\n\n## Parity and keys\n\nThe adapter generates deterministic keys from tree positions. Core SSR output is tested against the HTML renderer. Custom components, raw HTML, highlighter output, and HTML-only extension hooks are application-controlled boundaries and are not covered by that equivalence guarantee.\n"}
